WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.950
Which cloud?

2
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.652
For this estate, a GCC tenant,

3
00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:07.757
every Graph read and write goes to the
worldwide endpoint, and the three Graph calls

4
00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:12.788
this chapter writes with are all listed
for the government service levels as well.

5
00:00:12.788 --> 00:00:17.130
The code takes the host from its cloud
table and checks it on every request,

6
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.687
which matters because Learn's tutorial
simply hard-codes the worldwide host.

7
00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:26.791
On the directory side, the disables go only
to the domain you name, and one detail

8
00:00:26.791 --> 00:00:32.110
to remember: the disable command won't work
against a read-only domain controller.
